!-- Map Room banner 728x90 top -->\n   <ins class=\"adsbygoogle\" data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-0798734761149428\" data-ad-slot=\"[PHONE REDACTED]\" data-adsbygoogle-status=\"done\" style=\"display:inline-block;width:728px;height:90px\">\n    <div aria-label=\"Advertisement\" id=\"aswift_0_host\" style=\"border: none; height: 90px; width: 728px; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; position: relative; visibility: visible; background-color: transparent; display: inline-block;\" tabindex=\"0\" title=\"Advertisement\">\n    </div>\n   </ins>\n  </div>\n  <header>\n   <div id=\"banner-title\">\n    <div id=\"search\">\n     <form action=\"\" id=\"cse-search-box\">\n      <div>\n       <input name=\"cx\" type=\"hidden\" value=\"partner-pub-0798734761149428:q50b0d9oonb\">\n       <input name=\"cof\" type=\"hidden\" value=\"FORID:10\">\n       <input name=\"ie\" type=\"hidden\" value=\"UTF-8\">\n       <input id=\"searchtext\" name=\"q\" placeholder size=\"31\" style='background: url(\"\") left 9px top 50% no-repeat rgb(255, 255, 255);' type=\"text\">\n      </div>\n      <input name=\"siteurl\" type=\"hidden\" value=\"archives.maproomblog.com/2006/05/book_review_walking_with_your_ancestors_by_melinda_kashuba.php\">\n      <input name=\"ref\" type=\"hidden\" value>\n      <input name=\"ss\" type=\"hidden\" value>\n     </form>\n    </div>\n    <h1>\n     <a>\n      The Map Room\n     </a>\n    </h1>\n    <h2>\n     A Weblog About Maps\n    </h2>\n    <nav>\n     <ul id=\"menu\">\n      <li class=\"menu-item\">\n       <a>\n        About The Map Room\n       </a>\n      </li>\n      <li class=\"menu-item\">\n       <a>\n        The Archives\n       </a>\n      </li>\n      <li class=\"menu-item\">\n       <a>\n        The Most Recent Posts\n       </a>\n      </li>\n      <li class=\"menu-item\">\n       <a>\n        The Fantasy Maps Project\n       </a>\n      </li>\n     </ul>\n    </nav>\n   </div>\n  </header>\n  <div id=\"content\">\n   <!-- google_ad_section_start -->\n   <article class=\"entry\">\n    <h1 class=\"entry-title\">\n     Book Review: Walking with Your Ancestors by Melinda Kashuba\n    </h1>\n    <div class=\"entry-text\">\n     <p>\n      <b>\n       <a>\n        Walking with Your Ancestors: A Genealogist&rsquo;s Guide to Using Maps and Geography\n       </a>\n       <br>\n       by Melinda Kashuba\n       <br>\n       Family Tree Books, 2005.\n      </b>\n     </p>\n     <p>\n      <a>\n       <img src=\"rick.jpg\" style=\"border: 0; float: right; margin: 0.3em 0 0.7em 1.5em; height: 239px; width: 184px\">\n      </a>\n      I do other things besides this web site; one of these is to volunteer at the local archives, a private organization covering the surrounding county that&rsquo;s based in my town.\n     </p>\n     <p>\n      It&rsquo;s that very question, hypothetical though it may be in my case, that Melinda Kashuba&rsquo;s book,\n      <i>\n       <a>\n        Walking with Your Ancestors: A Genealogist&rsquo;s Guide to Using Maps and Geography\n       </a>\n      </i>\n      , answers. While Kashuba, a genealogical researcher with a Ph.D. in geographer, has the genealogical audience in mind, this book could, with a slight change in focus, easily serve as a general introduction to old maps held in American archives &mdash; how they were made, how to read them, and how to use them in your research.\n     </p>\n     <p>\n      In slightly more than two hundred pages, Kashuba covers a lot of ground. We get a lot about how to read old maps &mdash; including how to use a gazetteer, which is basic, and how to track down place names that may have changed or moved, which is not.\n     </p>\n     <p>\n      In her introduction, Kashuba argues that\n      <em>\n       geography\n      </em>\n      is more important to genealogy than\n      <em>\n       history\n      </em>\n      is &mdash; an ostensibly strange argument, but it&rsquo;s hard to refute her assertion that place is central to genealogical research:\n     </p>\n     <blockquote>\n      Genealogy is a geographically driven subject.\n      <em>\n       as\n      </em>\n      important if not\n      <em>\n       more\n      </em>\n      important than history to the genealogist. Knowing where your ancestors lived is the key to finding &ldquo;the really good stuff&rdquo; in those records.\n     </blockquote>\n     <p>\n      True enough, many of the researchers I&rsquo;ve encountered have had trouble tracking down a name because they weren&rsquo;t sure where to look. Adding maps to the search can suggest other avenues: if your great-great grandfather isn&rsquo;t in this town, perhaps he&rsquo;s in the town down the river &mdash; or perhaps he&rsquo;s got records at the county seat.\n     </p>\n     <p>\n      Unfortunately, this book won&rsquo;t be of much help in my archives; Kashuba&rsquo;s book is American in scope. But this accessible, engaging book will no doubt be useful to genealogists across the U.S., and should probably be in every local archive&rsquo;s reference shelf.\n     </p>\n     <p>\n      I received a review copy of this book.\n      <a>\n       More on my book review policy\n      </a>\n      .\n     </p>\n     <footer>\n      <div class=\"entry-footer\">\n       <p>\n        posted to\n        <a>\n         Book Reviews\n        </a>\n        |\n        <time class=\"entry-date\" datetime=\"2006-05-08T11:09:54-05:00\" pubdate=\"pubdate\">\n         May  8, 2006\n        </time>\n       </p>\n      </div>\n     </footer>\n    </div>\n    <!-- /entry-text -->\n   </article>\n   <nav>\n    <ul class=\"entry-nav\">\n     <li>\n      <a title=\"Think Globally, Act Regionally: GIS for the Social Sciences\">\n       &laquo; prev\n      </a>\n     </li>\n     <li>\n      <a title=\"Alaska's North Slope\">\n       next &raquo;\n      </a>\n     </li>\n    </ul>\n   </nav>\n   <aside>\n    <div class=\"blog-entry-share\" id=\"share-927\">\n     <span class=\"blog-entry-facebook\">\n     </span>\n     <span class=\"blog-entry-twitter\">\n     </span>\n    </div>\n   </aside>\n   <div id=\"ad-inline\">\n    <!-- Map Room individual entry, 336x280 -->\n    <ins class=\"adsbygoogle\" data-ad-client=\"ca-pub-0798734761149428\" data-ad-slot=\"[PHONE REDACTED]\" data-adsbygoogle-status=\"done\" style=\"display: inline-block; width: 336px; height: 0px;\">\n     <div aria-label=\"Advertisement\" id=\"aswift_1_host\" style=\"border: none; height: 0px; width: 336px; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; position: relative; visibility: visible; background-color: transparent; display: inline-block; overflow: hidden; opacity: 0;\" tabindex=\"0\" title=\"Advertisement\">\n     </div>\n    </ins>\n   </div>\n   <div id=\"comments\">\n    <h2 id=\"comments-title\">\n     Comments\n    </h2>\n    <div id=\"disqus_recommendations\" style=\"margin-bottom: 12px;\">\n    </div>\n    <div id=\"disqus_thread\">\n    </div>\n    <noscript>\n     <p id=\"comments-noscript\">\n      Please enable JavaScript to view the\n      <a>\n       comments powered by Disqus.\n      </a>\n     </p>\n    </noscript>\n    <p id=\"comments-footer\">\n    </p>\n   </div>\n   <!-- /comments -->\n   <!-- google_ad_section_end -->\n  </div>\n  <!-- /content -->\n  <div id=\"sidebar\">\n   <h2>\n    <a>\n     About The Map Room\n    </a>\n   </h2>\n   <a>\n    <img alt=\"Jonathan Crowe\" id=\"profile-pic\" src=\"rick.jpg\">\n   </a>\n   <p>\n    <b>\n     The Map Room\n    </b>\n    is a blog about maps by\n    <a>\n     Jonathan Crowe\n    </a>\n    , covering everything from collecting to the latest in geospatial technology.\n   </p>\n   <p>\n    It returned in January 2016 after a four-year hiatus.\n   </p>\n   <!--\n\t\n\t<h2><a >The Archives</a></h2>\n\n\t<p>During <b>The Map Room</b>’s eight-year run, I posted a total of 4,055 entries. You can explore them by visiting the <a >archives</a>:</p>\n\n\t<nav>\n\t<form id=\"sidebar-categories\">\n\t\t<select onchange=\"makelinkto(this);\">\n\t\t\t<option value=\"\">Select category:</option>\n\t